return [====[assage. Its name begins “Skeleton of” and comes from the same name generator as your Hero. Its abilities, identity perks, class growth, health dice and eligible automatic feats use the ordinary Hero framework, with AI choices restricted to abilities its controller can use.</p><p>The Fighter closes in for melee, the Rogue fires SMG bursts, and the Wizard warns before striking a ground arc. Wizard arcs spend 12 base Magic plus their Content cost, modified by ordinary offensive Magic rules. Wizards cycle their generated Contents and must regenerate when their Magic runs low. Shared defenses, status effects and class rules still apply.</p><p>The Skeleton is always on the approachable side of its barrier. Fight it before crossing. A legitimate defeat opens the tall barrier for every Hero, including later arrivals; your normal keycard, boss and rescue sequence remains intact. Regenerating the dungeon creates a fresh encounter.</p><p>Combat XP follows ordinary killing-blow and damage-contribution rules, and normal individualized enemy drops apply. There is no extra cash, DFT or guaranteed equipment award. Removing the enemy is not a combat victory.</p><p>Administrator preview: lod_event_preview_generate skeleton_blockade. Redeploy and follow the printed location. The preview is unranked.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 87</div></article><article class="page" id="fallen-heroes" data-title="Your bones remember"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>Your bones remember</h2><table><tr><td>When a player dies</td><td>Their build returns as an enemy AI skeleton.</td></tr><tr><td>Before it attacks</td><td>Three seconds of rattling bones and a violet warning.</td></tr><tr><td>After respawning</td><td>Your skeleton is still out there. Protect each other.</td></tr></table><p>A death in the active dungeon leaves a named skeleton near the fallen player. This happens even when dungeon events are switched off. It copies the identity, class, level, abilities, feats, equipment, weapons and remaining resources of the body that died, and rises at full copied maximum health. A fallen player-controlled Soldier copies that Soldier incarnation.</p><p>The skeleton uses its copied weapons and spells against the Heroes. Firearms spend copied ammunition; Wands spend copied charges; spells spend and regenerate Magic. A copied Soldier retains the Soldier rifle’s unlimited ammunition. Wall and Summon spells belong to the enemy side too. Red attack warnings give you time to react.</p><p>These are independent copies. Changing gear, respawning or disconnecting cannot weaken or erase them. Their duplicated gear cannot be looted, and defeating them awards no experience or other kill rewards. Ordinary event Skeletons still have their normal combat rewards.</p><p>Defeat your own skeleton to lay your bones to rest, or avenge a teammate. Staging deaths and deaths after dungeon completion create no skeleton. All remaining copies clear when the dungeon ends. If a death site is blocked, the skeleton waits for a safe nearby place to rise.</p><blockquote>“Keep your friends alive. You already know how dangerous their builds are.”<br>— Deborah</blockquote><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 88</div></article><article class="page" id="equipment-quiz" data-title="The Game Master: know what you wear"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>The Game Master: know what you wear</h2><table><tr><td>Before accepting</td><td>One attempt per account per dungeon. Decline freely.</td></tr><tr><td>Correct answer</td><td>One DFT, only when collection succeeds.</td></tr><tr><td>Wrong answer</td><td>The real worn item is stolen.</td></tr><tr><td>Time limit</td><td>30 seconds after acceptance; the dungeon keeps running.</td></tr></table><p>A suspiciously familiar grin waits in an optional hidden alcove. Press E at the Game Master and read his offer. You have 30 seconds to accept. Your task is to identify one piece of equipment you are wearing among two plausible phonies. The three cards show names, slots and properties. You cannot consult Equipment, Character Sheet, Wallet or the other Player Menu pages while answering.</p><p>Only ordinary procedural wearables are at risk. Weapons, consumables, protected or bound gear, free starting items and DFT-created equipment are excluded. Paired gloves count as one item and occupy both hands. No eligible equipment, a full eight-token DFT collection or unavailable reward storage means no accepted attempt.</p><p>Answer within 30 seconds. A wrong submitted answer removes the selected real item and its equipment effects. Cancelling, closing, timing out, dying, disconnecting, moving out of range or line of sight, or losing the current challenge forfeits the attempt without theft or reward. The world does not pause or protect you.</p><p>A correct answer earns one persistent, server-local DFT with no cash value. If storage fails after your answer, the result reads pending rather than success. Your menus reopen; use the same Game Master to retry the same frozen reward while the same Hero life, worn item and dungeon remain valid. Losing that binding forfeits an uncollected reward.</p><p>The Game Master disappears for you after your attempt ends. Other Heroes retain their own independent attempt and may play simultaneously. Reconnecting, changing Heroes or regenerating this dungeon does not grant another attempt. A new dungeon does. Late arrivals see the encounter appropriate to their own account.</p><p>Administrator preview: lod_event_preview_generate equipment_quiz. Redeploy with eligible ordinary wearable equipment and follow the printed locator. The preview is unranked but confirmed play risks actual equipment and awards a persistent DFT.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 89</div></article><article class="page" id="encounter-ecology" data-title="The prison changes its company"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>The prison changes its company</h2><p>Each dungeon draws its ordinary encounter squads from a tactical theme: Hunting Grounds, Occupation, Corruption, Crossfire, Quarantine or Funeral Retinue. Hunters pursue and ambush; occupation mixes guards and enforcers; corruption brings strange attacks; crossfire fills firing lanes; quarantine controls space; funeral retinues pair specialists with allies.</p><p>The prison avoids its two most recent themes and favors unfamiliar squads. Directed encounters draw from a themed selection, while roaming monsters use a much broader shared cast with extra weight for the dungeon’s favored types. A theme is not a promise that every wandering enemy will be the same few kinds. Keycard guards keep their own authored rules.</p><p>Roaming populations also change with the dungeon: Corruption favors Deadcrabs and Bio Blasters, Crossfire favors ranged bodies, Hunting Grounds favors Runners, Occupation favors Soldiers, and Funeral Retinue favors Shamblers. A few independent specialists can join them: Siphoners, Caromers, Reapers, Redliners, Drubbers and Afterbursts. Support teams, linked pairs, fixed traps and bosses remain in authored encounters. Roamers travel alone; their presence is not a promise of an escort.</p><p>Hunting Grounds and Occupation aim for twenty living roamers per physical floor; other themes aim for eighteen. The prison never budgets more than sixty-four roamers in total, so four-floor dungeons aim for sixteen per floor. Up to eight roamers on a floor may be distinct specialists, without duplicate living roaming specialists of one kind. A dead monster’s vacancy gets an opportunity about every twenty seconds, and some themes leave it empty longer. Initial positions that could not be filled retry separately, without replaying missed spawns. New bodies need clear supported homes away from Heroes and protected objectives, plus a usable patrol exit; full or obstructed areas wait rather than force a spawn.</p><p>The shape of the prison influences which squads fit: ambushers favor corners, pursuit units favor alternate routes, and firing teams favor clear straight approaches. Vertical approaches can attract Climbers; junctions and approaches to keycards can favor support squads. These are tendencies, not guarantees. Ordinary encounter groups leave space between their home positions, though wandering or pursuing enemies can still converge.</p><p>Sectors have a rhythm along the route from their entrance toward the keycard or the approachable side of the Black Gate: brief quiet stretches, lighter probes, pressure and a short recovery approach. Ordinary fights and patrol homes favor the routes you traverse, while deeper branches retain surprises. Entrance and goal respite bands are short, not whole empty regions. Hunting Grounds favors ambush phrases, Occupation and Crossfire pressure, and Funeral Retinue surges or ambushes; every rhythm remains possible. Probes keep their characteristic enemies and companions, with fewer extra bodies as party size and dungeon level grow. Keycard fights retain their own rules. Beyond the protected dungeon opening, wandering, pursuit, backtracking and separated teammates can still interrupt ordinary sector respite. The entrance sanctuary and its shared opening-pressure limit remain separate protections.</p><p>A theme changes how often enemies can arrive, and therefore your opportunity to meet an Elite; it does not change an individual enemy’s tier roll. Every ordinary body still rolls 60% Typical, 30% Elite or 10% Champion. Tells, weaknesses, rewards and abilities keep their own rules. Read each encounter: companions, cover and escape routes still matter. A new campaign starts a new encounter history.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 90</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_academic_achievement" data-title="Academic Achievement"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Academic Achievement</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_ACADEMIC_ACHIEVEMENT"><h3>Academic Achievement</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / magic_pool</p><p>Add your positive CHA modifier to your INT modifier when calculating passive Magic regeneration. Regeneration must be permitted.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 91</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_aggressive_personality" data-title="Aggressive Personality"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Aggressive Personality</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_AGGRESSIVE_PERSONALITY"><h3>Aggressive Personality</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / eligible physical attack</p><p>Your next physical attack adds your positive CHA modifier as damage to each target. Cooldown: 1d3 seconds; these timing dice do not explode.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 92</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_aura_burst" data-title="Aura Burst"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Aura Burst</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_AURA_BURST_1"><h3>Aura Burst</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>When you successfully spend Magic on a discrete action, deal your positive CHA modifier as extra Magic damage to enemies within 0 same-floor cells. Sustained drain does not trigger this.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with a discrete active Magic Form</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_RADIANCE_2"><h3>Radiance</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Aura Burst</p><p>When you successfully spend Magic on a discrete action, deal your positive CHA modifier as extra Magic damage to enemies within 1 same-floor cells. Sustained drain does not trigger this. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with a discrete active Magic Form</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_MAJESTY_3"><h3>Majesty</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Radiance</p><p>When you successfully spend Magic on a discrete action, deal your positive CHA modifier as extra Magic damage to enemies within 2 same-floor cells. Sustained drain does not trigger this. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with a discrete active Magic Form</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 93</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_hitstun_presence" data-title="Unnerving Presence"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Unnerving Presence</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_HITSTUN_1"><h3>Unnerving Presence</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Increase hit stun you inflict by 22% after CHA scaling. Resistance, retrigger protection and duration caps still apply.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible hit-stun source</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_HITSTUN_2"><h3>Dazing Presence</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Unnerving Presence</p><p>Increase hit stun you inflict by 44% after CHA scaling. Resistance, retrigger protection and duration caps still apply. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible hit-stun source</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_HITSTUN_3"><h3>Overwhelming Presence</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Dazing Presence</p><p>Increase hit stun you inflict by 66% after CHA scaling. Resistance, retrigger protection and duration caps still apply. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible hit-stun source</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 94</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_intimidation_proc" data-title="Daunting"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Daunting</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_FEAR_PROC_1"><h3>Daunting</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Your damaging hit has a 11% chance to force a surviving target to check Morale. Requires its Morale cooldown to be ready; skips hits that already force a check.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_FEAR_PROC_2"><h3>Cowing</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Daunting</p><p>Your damaging hit has a 22% chance to force a surviving target to check Morale. Requires its Morale cooldown to be ready; skips hits that already force a check. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_FEAR_PROC_3"><h3>Overawing</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Cowing</p><p>Your damaging hit has a 33% chance to force a surviving target to check Morale. Requires its Morale cooldown to be ready; skips hits that already force a check. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 95</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_menace" data-title="Menacing"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Menacing</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_MENACE_1"><h3>Menacing</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Gain +2 Morale DC. A hit exceeding 30% of a human target’s MaxHP can trigger Morale; low HP alone cannot.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_MENACE_2"><h3>Dreadful</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Menacing</p><p>Gain +4 Morale DC. A hit exceeding 25% of a human target’s MaxHP can trigger Morale; low HP alone cannot. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_MENACE_3"><h3>Terrifying</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Dreadful</p><p>Gain +4 Morale DC. A hit exceeding 20% of a human target’s MaxHP can trigger Morale; low HP alone cannot. Each target’s first Morale save against you per encounter rolls twice and keeps the lower die. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 96</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_nerve" data-title="Iron Nerve"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Iron Nerve</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_NERVE_1"><h3>Iron Nerve</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Gain +2 to Morale saves.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors subject to Morale</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_NERVE_2"><h3>Unbreakable Nerve</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Iron Nerve</p><p>Gain +4 to Morale saves. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors subject to Morale</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 97</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_panic" data-title="Panic Is Contagious"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Panic Is Contagious</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_PANIC"><h3>Panic Is Contagious</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Dreadful</p><p>When an enemy fails Morale against you, AI enemies below half HP within 2 connected cells make a Morale check. This cannot cascade again; each target is immune to cascades for 3 seconds.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 98</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_personality_aura" data-title="Abrasive Personality"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Abrasive Personality</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_ABRASIVE_PERSONALITY_1"><h3>Abrasive Personality</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Every 3 seconds, deal your positive CHA modifier as untyped damage to enemies within 0 same-floor cells. Wait the full initial interval; no catch-up pulses.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_NARCISSISM_2"><h3>Narcissism</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Abrasive Personality</p><p>Every 3 seconds, deal your positive CHA modifier as untyped damage to enemies within 1 same-floor cells. Wait the full initial interval; no catch-up pulses. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_MEGALOMANIA_3"><h3>Megalomania</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Narcissism</p><p>Every 3 seconds, deal your positive CHA modifier as untyped damage to enemies within 2 same-floor cells. Wait the full initial interval; no catch-up pulses. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 99</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_self_actualization" data-title="Self-Actualization"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Self-Actualization</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_SELF_ACTUALIZATION"><h3>Self-Actualization</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / eligible Magic Form</p><p>Add your positive CHA modifier to each target’s magical damage, once after damage multipliers.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 100</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_winning_personality" data-title="Winning Personality"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Winning Personality</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_WINNING_PERSONALITY"><h3>Winning Personality</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17</p><p>Gain +1 intrinsic CHA, up to the ability ceiling. Use the higher of INT or CHA to meet INT feat ability requirements. Other prerequisites still apply.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 101</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_big_guy" data-title="Big Guy"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Big Guy</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_BIG_GUY"><h3>Big Guy</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15 and STR 13</p><p>Your body and hurt volume become 30% larger. Gain 15% melee reach and 20% physical push dealt. Your movement hull stays the same. Incompatible with Little Guy.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 102</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_blast_proof" data-title="Blast-Proof"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Blast-Proof</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_BLAST_PROOF"><h3>Blast-Proof</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15</p><p>Stop the first continuation of an incoming exploding damage chain. Keep damage already rolled; other chains continue normally. Cooldown: 2 seconds.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 103</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_glow_up" data-title="Glow Up"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Glow Up</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_GLOW_UP"><h3>Glow Up</h3><p class="requirement">CON 17 / requires a usable explicit CHA_MOD-derived damage source</p><p>Whenever your own ability adds your positive CHA modifier as damage, also add your positive CON modifier once to that damage event.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an authored CHA_MOD-derived damage source</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 104</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_health_regeneration" data-title="Second Wind"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Second Wind</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_REGEN_11"><h3>Second Wind</h3><p class="requirement">CON 13</p><p>After 5 damage-free seconds, regenerate 1% MaxHP per second, scaled by CON. Add 22% MaxHP to your regeneration ceiling; this stacks with Fighter’s innate 33% and cannot restore Tetris overfill.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CON_REGEN_22"><h3>Rapid Recovery</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15 / requires Second Wind</p><p>After 5 damage-free seconds, regenerate 2% MaxHP per second, scaled by CON. Add 44% MaxHP to your regeneration ceiling; this stacks with Fighter’s innate 33% and cannot restore Tetris overfill. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CON_REGEN_33"><h3>Unbroken</h3><p class="requirement">CON 17 / requires Rapid Recovery</p><p>After 5 damage-free seconds, regenerate 2% MaxHP per second, scaled by CON. Add 66% MaxHP to your regeneration ceiling; this stacks with Fighter’s innate 33% and cannot restore Tetris overfill. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 105</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_not_yet" data-title="Not Yet"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Not Yet</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_NOT_YET"><h3>Not Yet</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15</p><p>Once per dungeon, lethal damage received above 1 HP leaves you at 1 HP and grants 0.5 seconds of damage immunity. Death, respawn and reconnect do not restore this use.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 106</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_poison_proc" data-title="Venomous"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Venomous</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_POISON_PROC_1"><h3>Venomous</h3><p class="requirement">CON 13</p><p>Your hit has a 11% chance to attempt Poisoned. The target saves with CON against your CON modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="CON_POISON_PROC_2"><h3>Toxic</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15 / requires Venomous</p><p>Your hit has a 22% chance to attempt Poisoned. The target saves with CON against your CON modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="CON_POISON_PROC_3"><h3>Virulent</h3><p class="requirement">CON 17 / requires Toxic</p><p>Your hit has a 33% chance to attempt Poisoned. The target saves with CON against your CON modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 107</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_steadfast" data-title="Hard to Move"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Hard to Move</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_STEADFAST"><h3>Hard to Move</h3><p class="requirement">CON 13</p><p>Reduce ordinary hit-stun duration and incoming push distance by 25%. Scripted boss effects may ignore this resistance.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 108</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_big_scary" data-title="Big Scary"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Big Scary</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_BIG_SCARY"><h3>Big Scary</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15, STR 13, and CHA 15 / Big Guy; Menacing</p><p>Gain +2 Morale DC when dealing melee damage, physical push or wall-crush damage. This stacks with Menacing.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 109</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_boom_battery" data-title="Boom Battery"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Boom Battery</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_BOOM_BATTERY"><h3>Boom Battery</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 and INT 15 / Capability: exploding_nonmagic_damage_dice</p><p>Every second continuation die in a non-Magic attack restores 1 Magic. Maximum: 5 Magic per attack; never above 100 Magic.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, Magic-using AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 110</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_crush_panic" data-title="Crash the Party"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Crash the Party</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_CRUSH_PANIC"><h3>Crash the Party</h3><p class="requirement">STR 17 and CHA 17 / Pusher; Dreadful</p><p>Your wall crush forces an eligible target to check Morale, even during its normal recheck cooldown. Once per target every 3 seconds.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with physical push</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 111</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_force_of_will" data-title="Force of Will"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Force of Will</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_FORCE_OF_WILL"><h3>Force of Will</h3><p class="requirement">STR 15 and WIS 15 / Pusher; Force Multiplier</p><p>Magic that already pushes can trigger Pusher, Shover or Space Hog after Force Multiplier. A successful proc adds 168 units and uses your Pusher wall-slam die. Shared per-target cooldown: 0.5 seconds.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, eligible AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 112</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_meteor_strike" data-title="Meteor Strike"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Meteor Strike</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_METEOR_STRIKE"><h3>Meteor Strike</h3><p class="requirement">STR 15 and INT 15 / Bash; Cloud Step</p><p>After using Cloud Step, your first Crowbar hit before landing adds one exploding d6 and doubles its Crowbar push. A miss does not consume this strike. Landing resets it.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes/human Soldiers with Crowbar-family access</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 113</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_tiny_terror" data-title="Tiny Terror"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Tiny Terror</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_TINY_TERROR"><h3>Tiny Terror</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 and CHA 15 / Little Guy; Menacing</p><p>While Little Guy is active, gain +2 Morale DC against enemies within 2 connected cells. This stacks with Menacing.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 114</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_burst_size" data-title="Extra Round"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Extra Round</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_BURSTER_1"><h3>Extra Round</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Add 1 rounds to existing multi-shot bursts at their normal spacing and damage, with no extra ammunition cost. Single shots and Shotgun pellets are not bursts.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors with an authored weapon attack tagged multiFireBurst</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_BURSTER_2"><h3>Extended Volley</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Extra Round</p><p>Add 2 rounds to existing multi-shot bursts at their normal spacing and damage, with no extra ammunition cost. Single shots and Shotgun pellets are not bursts. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors with an authored weapon attack tagged multiFireBurst</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_BURSTER_3"><h3>Full Barrage</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Extended Volley</p><p>Add 3 rounds to existing multi-shot bursts at their normal spacing and damage, with no extra ammunition cost. Single shots and Shotgun pellets are not bursts. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors with an authored weapon attack tagged multiFireBurst</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 115</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_clumsy_proc" data-title="Distracting"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Distracting</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_CLUMSY_PROC_1"><h3>Distracting</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Your hit has a 11% chance to attempt Clumsy. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_CLUMSY_PROC_2"><h3>Disorienting</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Distracting</p><p>Your hit has a 22% chance to attempt Clumsy. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_CLUMSY_PROC_3"><h3>Discombobulating</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Disorienting</p><p>Your hit has a 33% chance to attempt Clumsy. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 116</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_exploding_damage_dice" data-title="Perfect Ten"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Perfect Ten</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_EXPLODE_D10"><h3>Perfect Ten</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Your ordinary d10 damage dice explode on their maximum face. Continuations explode at 10 minus BoomShift, minimum 2. Maximum: 32 dice per chain. Earlier die unlocks remain active.</p><p class="actors">Non-Rogue heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with d10 damage rolls</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_EXPLODE_D8"><h3>Eight Is Enough</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Perfect Ten</p><p>Your ordinary d8 damage dice explode on their maximum face. Continuations explode at 8 minus BoomShift, minimum 2. Maximum: 32 dice per chain. Earlier die unlocks remain active.</p><p class="actors">Non-Rogue heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with d8 damage rolls</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_EXPLODE_D4"><h3>Fourtunate</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Eight Is Enough</p><p>Your ordinary d4 damage dice explode on their maximum face. Continuations explode at 4 minus BoomShift, minimum 2. Maximum: 32 dice per chain. Earlier die unlocks remain active.</p><p class="actors">Non-Rogue heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with d4 damage rolls</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 117</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_immolate_proc" data-title="Singeing"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Singeing</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_IMMOLATE_PROC_1"><h3>Singeing</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Your hit has a 11% chance to attempt Immolated. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_IMMOLATE_PROC_2"><h3>Scorching</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Singeing</p><p>Your hit has a 22% chance to attempt Immolated. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_IMMOLATE_PROC_3"><h3>Incendiary</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Scorching</p><p>Your hit has a 33% chance to attempt Immolated. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 118</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_magnum_deadeye" data-title="Deadeye"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Deadeye</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_MAGNUM_DEADEYE"><h3>Deadeye</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15</p><p>Stand perfectly still for 0.5 seconds to empower your next primary attack: double damage with a standard weapon, or triple damage with the .357 Magnum. One attack consumes the aim.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled actors using a standard player weapon</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 119</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_rate_of_fire" data-title="Hair Trigger"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Hair Trigger</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_RATE_OF_FIRE_1"><h3>Hair Trigger</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Increase ordinary firearm primary-fire rate by 10%. Reloads, cooling, targeting windups and spacing within bursts stay unchanged.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI whose equipped/authored ordinary firearm uses the shared attack-cadence authority</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_RATE_OF_FIRE_2"><h3>Rapid Fire</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Hair Trigger</p><p>Increase ordinary firearm primary-fire rate by 20%. Reloads, cooling, targeting windups and spacing within bursts stay unchanged. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI whose equipped/authored ordinary firearm uses the shared attack-cadence authority</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_RATE_OF_FIRE_3"><h3>Lead Storm</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Rapid Fire</p><p>Increase ordinary firearm primary-fire rate by 30%. Reloads, cooling, targeting windups and spacing within bursts stay unchanged. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI whose equipped/authored ordinary firearm uses the shared attack-cadence authority</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 120</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_reload_cadence" data-title="Quick Reload"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Quick Reload</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_FAST_RELOAD"><h3>Quick Reload</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Reduce ordinary weapon reload time by 20%. This does not shorten SMG cooling or attack windups.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes/human Soldiers; AI only when its authored weapon uses the shared reload authority</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_FAST_RELOAD_2"><h3>Lightning Reload</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Quick Reload</p><p>Reduce ordinary weapon reload time by 40%. This does not shorten SMG cooling or attack windups. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes/human Soldiers; AI only when its authored weapon uses the shared reload authority</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_FAST_RELOAD_3"><h3>Blink Reload</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Lightning Reload</p><p>Reduce ordinary weapon reload time by 60%. This does not shorten SMG cooling or attack windups. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes/human Soldiers; AI only when its authored weapon uses the shared reload authority</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 121</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_shrink" data-title="Little Guy"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Little Guy</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_SHRINK"><h3>Little Guy</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15</p><p>Your visible body becomes 30% smaller. Your movement hull, weapon traces and interaction reach stay the same. Incompatible with Big Guy.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 122</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_smg_heat" data-title="Cold Hands"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Cold Hands</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_SMG_COLD_HANDS_1"><h3>Cold Hands</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Each SMG round has a 11% chance to add no heat. Overheat threshold: 8. Overheating still locks firing for 2 seconds.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers who possess/use the SMG</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_SMG_COLD_HANDS_2"><h3>Ice in the Veins</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Cold Hands</p><p>Each SMG round has a 22% chance to add no heat. Overheat threshold: 10. Overheating still locks firing for 2 seconds. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers who possess/use the SMG</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_SMG_COLD_HANDS_3"><h3>Absolute Zero</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Ice in the Veins</p><p>Each SMG round has a 33% chance to add no heat. Overheat threshold: 12. Overheating still locks firing for 2 seconds. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers who possess/use the SMG</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 123</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_spring_heel" data-title="Spring Heel"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Spring Heel</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_SPRING_HEEL"><h3>Spring Heel</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Double the height of voluntary jumps, including Wall Jump and Cloud Step. Ceilings, wall-top barriers and locked routes still block travel.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 124</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_strafe" data-title="Strafer"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Strafer</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_STRAFER_1"><h3>Strafer</h3><p class="requirement"></p><p>Strafe 11% faster on the ground. Only the sideways component changes on diagonals. The ordinary speed cap still applies.</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_SIDELER_2"><h3>Sideler</h3><p class="requirement"></p><p>Strafe 22% faster on the ground. Only the sideways component changes on diagonals. The ordinary speed cap still applies. Replaces lower ranks.</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_LATERAL_MOVER_3"><h3>Lateral Mover</h3><p class="requirement"></p><p>Strafe 33% faster on the ground. Only the sideways component changes on diagonals. The ordinary speed cap still applies. Replaces lower ranks.</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 125</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_wall_jump" data-title="Wall Jump"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Wall Jump</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_WALL_JUMP"><h3>Wall Jump</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15</p><p>Press Jump within 24 units of a vertical wall to jump and kick away. Four uses before landing; no Magic cost. Spring Heel increases the jump height.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 126</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_ammo_regeneration_floor" data-title="Field Supply"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Field Supply</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_AMMO_FLOOR_44"><h3>Field Supply</h3><p class="requirement">INT 13</p><p>Owned regenerative firearm ammunition refills to 44% of family capacity, rounded up, with 22% faster per-round recovery. No-fire delay and capacity stay unchanged; no instant ammo, Wand charges, consumables or AR2 secondary ammo.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers with regenerative firearm ammunition</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_AMMO_FLOOR_55"><h3>Deep Reserves</h3><p class="requirement">INT 15 / requires Field Supply</p><p>Owned regenerative firearm ammunition refills to 55% of family capacity, rounded up, with 44% faster per-round recovery. No-fire delay and capacity stay unchanged; no instant ammo, Wand charges, consumables or AR2 secondary ammo. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers with regenerative firearm ammunition</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_AMMO_FLOOR_66"><h3>War Stock</h3><p class="requirement">INT 17 / requires Deep Reserves</p><p>Owned regenerative firearm ammunition refills to 66% of family capacity, rounded up, with 66% faster per-round recovery. No-fire delay and capacity stay unchanged; no instant ammo, Wand charges, consumables or AR2 secondary ammo. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers with regenerative firearm ammunition</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 127</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_arc_recovery" data-title="Arc Recovery"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Arc Recovery</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_ARC_RECOVERY"><h3>Arc Recovery</h3><p class="requirement">INT 17 / magic_pool</p><p>Kill an AI enemy with Magic damage to restore 11 Magic, up to 100. Cooldown: 2 seconds.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and Magic-using AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 128</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_arcane_disruption_proc" data-title="Disruptor"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Disruptor</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_ARCANE_PROC_1"><h3>Disruptor</h3><p class="requirement">INT 13</p><p>A nonmagical physical hit has a 11% chance to force a surviving target with an active Arcane Shield to make an INT Arcane Integrity save. Failure shatters the shield. Feedback from that hit resolves first.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_ARCANE_PROC_2"><h3>Spellbreaker</h3><p class="requirement">INT 15 / requires Disruptor</p><p>A nonmagical physical hit has a 22% chance to force a surviving target with an active Arcane Shield to make an INT Arcane Integrity save. Failure shatters the shield. Feedback from that hit resolves first. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_ARCANE_PROC_3"><h3>Nullifier</h3><p class="requirement">INT 17 / requires Spellbreaker</p><p>A nonmagical physical hit has a 33% chance to force a surviving target with an active Arcane Shield to make an INT Arcane Integrity save. Failure shatters the shield. Feedback from that hit resolves first. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 129</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_backpedal" data-title="W,A,S,Deborah"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>W,A,S,Deborah</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_WAS_DEBORAH"><h3>W,A,S,Deborah</h3><p class="requirement"></p><p>Move backward 25% faster, including backward diagonals. This affects voluntary ground movement and obeys the ordinary speed cap.</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 130</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_cloud_step" data-title="Cloud Step"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Cloud Step</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_CLOUD_STEP"><h3>Cloud Step</h3><p class="requirement">INT 13 / Magic pool</p><p>Once before landing, press Jump in the air for a 3-Magic extra jump with 2× takeoff impulse. Hold a direction for a horizontal boost. Invisible walls block maze shortcuts; Wall Jump takes priority.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 131</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_extracurricular_activity" data-title="Extracurricular Activity"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Extracurricular Activity</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_EXTRACURRICULAR_ACTIVITY"><h3>Extracurricular Activity</h3><p class="requirement">INT 17 / unowned Magic content</p><p>Learn one new Magic content immediately. Your later scheduled grants remain available.</p><p class="actors">Cooperative Heroes only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 132</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_feedback_loop" data-title="Feedback Loop"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Feedback Loop</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_FEEDBACK_LOOP"><h3>Feedback Loop</h3><p class="requirement">INT 15 / magic_pool</p><p>Each continuation die rolled by your offensive Magic restores 2 Magic. Maximum: 12 per cast, up to 100 Magic. Initial dice do not count.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and Magic-using AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 133</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_float_on" data-title="Float On"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Float On</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_FLOAT_ON"><h3>Float On</h3><p class="requirement">INT 15 / Magic pool</p><p>Once before landing, hold Jump at your apex to float for up to 6 seconds, spending 1 Magic per second. Release Jump, land or run out of Magic to end it.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 134</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_grand_unified_theory" data-title="Grand Unified Theory"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Grand Unified Theory</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_GRAND_UNIFIED_THEORY"><h3>Grand Unified Theory</h3><p class="requirement">INT 17 / unowned Magic form</p><p>Learn one new Magic form immediately. Your later scheduled grants remain available.</p><p class="actors">Cooperative Heroes only</p>]====]
